A||||6||DavidHenshaw||3.4 performance||||1||
Z||000000||DavidHenshaw||01-16-2001||01:02 PM||||The 3.4 is rated at about 160 hp. What can be done short of turbo or nitrous to increase the hp. and what are the gains in horsepower.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||bHooper||01-16-2001||01:16 PM||||do a search.  there is <B>plenty</B> of info about the 3.4 here.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||01-16-2001||06:57 PM||||Well with Dyno2000 and ported manifolds the Stock 3.4-liter OHV engine makes 166 horsepower @ 5000 rpm and 208-ft. lbs. of torque @ 3000-3500 rpm.<P>Add the GM performance 12363220 camshaft <A HREF="http://www.spoperformanceparts.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.spoperformanceparts.com</A>  and you get 169 horsepower @ 5000 rpm and 212-ft. lbs. of torque @ 3000 rpm.<P>Add ported heads to that from Norris Racing <A HREF="http://www.norrisracingtech.com/home.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.norrisracingtech.com/home.html</A>  and you get 178 horsepower @ 5000 rpm and 216-ft. lbs. of torque @ 3500 rpm.<P>Add the Silvolite 3409 <A HREF="http://www.kb-silvolite.com/slvpg24.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kb-silvolite.com/slvpg24.htm</A>  flat top pistons from the 3.4-liter TDC motor to that, which gives you 9.7-1 compression on the overhead valve motor and you get 185 horsepower @ 5000 rpm and 222 ft. lbs. of torque 3500 rpm.<P>Add headers like the FOCOA headers <A HREF="http://www.fieroowners.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroowners.com</A>  (NOT THE SPRINT MANIFOLDS) to that and you get 209 horsepower @ 5500 rpm and 236-ft. lbs. of torque @ 3500 rpm.<P>Add a 50-shot of nitrous to that and you get 259 horsepower @ 5500 rpm and 355-ft. lbs. of torque @ 2000 rpm. <P>Does that answer your question?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bill H||01-16-2001||08:23 PM||||hey 88formula does it make any differance if you have roller rockers? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||DavidHenshaw||01-17-2001||01:15 PM||||88Formula, I guess I owe you a six pack of your choice. That was excellent information. All I was wanting was about 200hp and it looks like the 3.4 can deliver in spades.<P>Dave <P>86 GT||||reg||1
