Z||000006||88formula||01-17-2001||05:24 PM||||Hey Bill, if you mean the full roller rocker arms with the roller fulcrum like the Crane Gold Race rocker arms than not really. Those rocker arms will give you about 5 horsepower and they are not worth spending $300-plus dollars. I know because I have them. They are cheap junk. The locks are known to come loose too.<P>Your better off staying with the stock rocker arms and if you need to replace them than the Comp Cams roller tip rocker arms are a good quality replacement for the stock rocker arms. They will not give you 15-20 horsepower like the company claims they will. I know this because a friend of mine who is a machinist has an engine dynamometer and he has tested those rocker arms to see what they give you for an increase in power on a smallblock Chevy engine over stock rocker arms (5 HP).<P><BR>DavidHenshaw, I like Sam Adams but I'll take anything including Guinness Stout (jk). If you know what you are going to do with your engine than I can give you an estimate of your 0-60 mph and quarter mile times.<BR>I can get the estimate pretty dam close to actual results with this program I have too. Just give me a holler.<P>For a baseline with this program I get 0-60 mph in 7.96 seconds and the quarter mile in 15.72 seconds @ 86 mph with a stock 5-speed fiero weighing 2925 lbs. with the driver. Most magazines that have tested the stock fiero get almost those same results with real tests.<P><BR>BHooper you don't have to be a member of FOCOA to get their headers. All you have to do is call them and they will sell them to you. If they don't I know some places that may have the FOCOA headers. <P><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 01-17-2001).]||||reg||1
